  "summary": "Four studies directly apply multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling (Bayesian hierarchical models) to customer churn prediction, making them the primary candidates. [V0209] (El-Sayed et al., 2021) applies this method to the ChurnBench dataset, reporting AUROC of 0.65. [V0212] (Haddad et al., 2024) applies the same method to AgriSat-4, reporting MAE of 0.86. [V0210] (Fischer et al., 2022) applies it to MetroFlow, reporting test F1 of 0.72. [V0211] (Gupta et al., 2023) applies it to Atlas-ICU, reporting accuracy of 0.79. These four are the directly relevant documents. A fifth slot is filled by [V0204] (Fischer et al., 2022), which applies decentralised training to customer attrition on AgriSat-4 (F1=0.64); it is on-topic for churn but uses a different method. Documents that only mention Bayesian hierarchical models as prior work (e.g., [V0009], [V0225], [V0183], [V0151]) are excluded as non-applications.",
